Title: Reconsider sitter toolbar placement as icon-position, not label-position
Created: 2026-09-06
Author: claude

--- log ---
2026-09-06T00:00Z claude created

--- body ---
## Context

Author, 2026-09-06: "Sa position naturelle dans l'UI pros and cons? A cote
de l'autre spinner, ou on laisse pres de la boite de recherche puisque
c'est l'index?" -- asked for a pros/cons on toolbar placement: beside the
existing sync spinner (global background activity) versus beside the
search box (where the button sits today, and where the thing it measures
-- the search index -- lives).

A first pass (Fable 5.1 synthesis, "Sitter's Ledger") recommended keeping
the current position, reasoning that only the items toolbar can carry the
text label "Index 43 %" the wording fix (0691) needs, and that the sync
area is icon-only "by design." On reflection that framing sets up a false
choice: it treats icon *position* and label *visibility* as the same
decision, when the ecosystem's own convention treats them as separate.

## What changes the picture

Zotero's sync spinner, and the `ProgressWindow` toast pattern most
widely-adopted plugins use (`zotero-plugin-toolkit` -- see 0693), both
show state through an icon plus an on-demand disclosure (tooltip, toast,
or the plugin's own dialog), not through permanent on-canvas text. That is
also the desktop-wide convention for background-job indicators (Dropbox,
iCloud, Time Machine menu-bar icons): the always-visible affordance is an
icon; the number appears on hover, click, or a transient toast. Under that
convention, "Index 43 %" does not need to live in the toolbar chrome at
all to satisfy 0691 -- it can live in a tooltip, an `aria-label` (which
also serves 0686's stable-accessible-name requirement), and the dialog's
first line, in *either* toolbar position.

This does not overturn the earlier recommendation, but it changes why it
holds. The pros/cons that still favor the items toolbar:

- **Host coupling.** The items-toolbar id is stable across Zotero 7-10;
  the sync button's internals changed between 6 and 7, so injecting beside
  it depends on more private layout.
- **Precedent.** Other index/full-text plugins already use the items
  toolbar; no known plugin injects beside the sync spinner.
- **Zero migration cost.** The button is already there.

What no longer favors either side, now that label-fitting is off the
table:

- Semantic/scope fit is genuinely closer for the sync area (global
  background activity) than for the items toolbar (per-library, per-
  collection scope) -- the earlier writeup called this a "mismatch" and
  proposed fixing it with tooltip wording; that fix is needed either way.

## Recommendation

Keep the current position for now -- host coupling and precedent are the
decisive, durable arguments, not the label-fitting argument that turns out
not to hold. Revisit only if the plugin moves toward icon+toast as its
primary interface (0693) and the extraction to its own repo (pending,
separate proposal) changes what "stable host coupling" even means for a
plugin no longer built as an in-tree experiment.

## Acceptance

- [ ] DECISIONS.md records this reasoning, explicitly superseding the
      earlier "only A can carry the label" justification with the
      host-coupling/precedent one.
- [ ] SPEC.md's placement wording (if any) reflects the corrected tooltip/
      scope fix: "Library: My Library -- Index 43 %", not "Index 43 %"
      alone.
